      "gap": "Supply the whole selected Feller II.9 presentation, not only its proof: the route omits the historical and justificatory claims of II.9, namely footnote 14 (the formula is James Stirling's, Methodus differentialis, 1730), footnote 16 (the usual proof that e^C = sqrt(2 pi) relies on Wallis's formula; Feller's simple direct proof in Amer. Math. Monthly 1967), footnote 15's citation of Robbins (Amer. Math. Monthly 62 (1955), 26-29; only the name survives in titles), and the p. 54 discussion of (9.15): the ratio of the extreme members is close to 1 - (12n^2)^{-1}, so the right member overestimates n! by an error of order n^{-2} per cent, and in reality much less (2.0007 at n = 2, 120.01 at n = 5). The proof, Robbins bounds, constant determination and footnote-17 refinement are present and complete. Text addressing these items exists only in the owned file handbook/parts/p15/distributions-transforms-and-moment-problems-w02c-p15-011.tex (not \\input on the route; route pending, not counted here).",
